      "dateCreated": "2026-10-19",
      "description": "Segmentation-free spatial cell-type mapping with SSAF-T for Xenium, MERSCOPE, CosMx, Visium HD and Stereo-seq data, from raw output folders or SpatialData .zarr. Transcripts or count bins become a kernel-density vector field; anchors sampled from the tissue are clustered and annotated by CeLLMan, run headless by Claude Code or Codex (optionally in reference mode); every voxel is assigned a cell type, filtered, and optionally cut into cells seeded by nuclei. A changed value re-runs only the stages it affects.",
      "gpu": "optional",
